{"copyright":{"thirdPartyPermissionsProduced":false,"disclosedToPublic":false,"approverComments":"Items in TRS are protected by copyright, but are furnished with U.S. government purpose use rights.","containsIndication":true,"publisherPermissionOrRightsToDistribute":false,"belongsToUsGov":false,"determinationType":"OTHER","thirdPartyContentCondition":"NOT_SET","belongsToContractor":false,"disclosedInvention":false,"submissionId":20230006986,"containsThirdPartyMaterial":false,"belongsToPublisher":true,"id":"36e9b0f3d52741f8a9496f648d51bf57","belongsToAuthors":false},"exportControl":{"isExportControl":"UNSET","submissionId":20230006986,"ear":"UNSET","id":"560f3f18cd7442b4be2ebbbf8a5d17b7","itar":"UNSET"},"created":"2022-01-03T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","distributionDate":"2022-01-03T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","center":{"code":"JPL","name":"Jet Propulsion Laboratory","id":"efbc9c123a0f47caafa95d99b7d2e1a1"},"onlyAbstract":false,"sensitiveInformation":0,"abstract":"The Mars 2020 Entry Descent and Landing (EDL) system delivered the Perseverance rover to the surface of Mars on February 18th, 2021. A large fraction of the Jezero Crater landing site was covered with landing hazards including cliffs, inescapable dune fields and rocks. These hazards were identified or inferred using orbital imagery before launch so that they could be avoided using Terrain Relative Navigation (TRN) which was composed of two parts: the Lander Vision System (LVS) and Safe Target Selection (STS). During EDL, the LVS successfully estimated map relative position by fusing landmarks matched between descent imagery and a map of the landing site with Inertial Measurement Unit (IMU) data. This position estimate was used by STS to identify the safest target for landing that was also reachable given fuel and other constraints. The EDL system then used the powered descent phase to retarget to this location and land safely. The overall error between the targeted location and actual landing location was 5m which was an order of magnitude less than the 60m touchdown error requirement. This paper will describe the final tests of the LVS before launch, the checkout of the LVS during operations and the LVS performance during EDL.","title":"Mars 2020 Lander Vision System Flight Performance 1","stiType":"PREPRINT","distribution":"PUBLIC","authorAffiliations":[{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230006986,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Zheng, Jason"}},"id":"f40ac8abe6e643cc9a94b94dd72d7af3"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230006986,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Shamah, Joe M."}},"id":"8e0ab89eaa5144fd850e4966ee271e54"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230006986,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Schaffner, Jacob"}},"id":"2f4b7b9e20a44bd89a96b702b3b22776"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230006986,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Ravine, Michael"}},"id":"47dcb75d2bb24ef8bc2622d3aefa68fe"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230006986,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Vaughan, Geoffrey"}},"id":"7cfaf336da2c4baf928804871a3d8767"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230006986,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Umsted, Carson"}},"id":"a4de4f2f31994064986e3b7705957440"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230006986,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Trawny, Nikolas"}},"id":"c23142a8fef64b6a96e7df1cae073020"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230006986,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Sun, George"}},"id":"01ddb5186259470bb058d633696c2724"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230006986,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Shenker, Boris"}},"id":"942fe3d7f35e483e90d83b1247b2ae82"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230006986,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Schroeder, Steven"}},"id":"3586e2a3e6524ce3ae88c5bf6c4cd540"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230006986,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Morrison, Jack"}},"id":"91631afe5aaa49cbb4d268ac040b7eb3"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230006986,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Montgomery, James F."}},"id":"a2e1bb2b93dc457a978e7cd5d178aece"},{"sequence":0,"submissionId":20230006986,"meta":{"author":{"name":"Mohan, Swati"}},"id":"6095840408654f5f9ebfb50ff56c8292"},{"seq